# Wave scheduler queue — one job per line. Copy this file and edit.
#
# Format:  <model_id>  <mode>  [library]  [wave_size]  [queue]  [flags]
#   model_id  : the model to run (its SIF must be at /shared/sif-files/<model_id>.sif)
#   mode      : ersilia | singularity
#   library   : full name or alias (real, molport, coconut, hit, liquid);
#               optional -> falls back to the driver's default_library arg
#   wave_size : 1..1000  (optional -> default 1000)
#   queue     : SLURM partition (optional -> default cpu-queue)
#   flags     : `hold` parks the job — the driver skips it until you unhold it.
#               `cpus=N` (1..32) pins SLURM cpus-per-task for THIS job only.
#               Flags are recognised by shape, so they can appear anywhere after
#               the model id: `eos3b5e ersilia coconut hold` is fine.
#
#   cpus=N is the packing lever. cpu-queue is CR_CPU — SLURM does no memory
#   accounting there — so cpus-per-task alone decides how many tasks share a
#   32-vCPU node, and a heavy model left at the default will OOM. Bigger N =
#   fewer tasks per node = more memory each = slower. Omit it to keep the
#   worker's own tuned default (ersilia 10, singularity 4).
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' (even indented) are ignored.
#
# ORDER IS PRIORITY. Jobs run top-to-bottom, one at a time; the next starts when
# the previous finishes. To prioritize a model, move its line up.
#
# THIS FILE IS LIVE. The driver re-reads it before every job, so you can edit it
# while the queue runs. Prefer sched-ctl.sh — it takes the same lock the driver
# uses and cannot leave a half-written file:
#
#   ./sched-ctl.sh add eos2r5a ersilia coconut --top   # queue it up next
#   ./sched-ctl.sh top eos74km_v1                      # prioritize
#   ./sched-ctl.sh hold eos6ojg_v1                     # park it
#   ./sched-ctl.sh cancel eos12x7_v1                   # stop the running model
#
# Hand-editing is supported too. A comment directly above a job line belongs to
# that job and moves with it when reordered; this banner always stays on top.

# --- examples (edit / delete) ---
eos4k4f_v1          ersilia      Enamine_Real_Sample_1.4B
eos2r5a             ersilia      Coconut_715K
mtb-public-models   singularity  molport                    500
# uses the driver's default_library (pass it as arg 2 to run-model-queue.sh):
# eos3b5e           ersilia

# parked until you run: sched-ctl.sh unhold eos12x7_v1
eos12x7_v1          ersilia      Enamine_Real_Sample_1.4B                     hold

# a memory-hungry model: 8 tasks/node instead of the default packing
eos11sm_v1          ersilia      Enamine_Real_Sample_1.4B                     cpus=4
eos6ojg_v1          ersilia      Enamine_Real_Sample_1.4B
eos74km_v1          ersilia      Enamine_Real_Sample_1.4B
eos42ez_v1          ersilia      Enamine_Real_Sample_1.4B
